# T-031 workbench Vercel deployment fix (2026-09-14).
#
# This repo doubles as the campaign EVIDENCE store: download/ alone carries
# 284 MB of durable evidence (dumps, tarballs, campaign batches, snapshots),
# and the tracked db/custom.db scaffold adds 20 MB. None of it is read by the
# Next.js app at runtime — but Vercel's file tracer pulled it all into the
# serverless function and the deployment died at:
#   "Required files read using Node.js fs library and node_modules exceed
#    max lambda size of 262144000 bytes"
# (every workbench deploy through 28e3ae9 failed this way, both projects).
#
# Runtime needs: src/, public/, data/review/** (the inferred read model),
# config files, package.json/bun.lock. Everything else is excluded here.
# Evidence durability is NOT affected: .vercelignore only shapes the upload,
# and the canonical evidence lives in git + GitHub releases (docs/RELEASING.md).
download/
db/
repos/
tool-results/
test-runs/
tests/
scripts/
examples/
mini-services/
docs/
